d to begin shortly in\nthe warned area.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nToh Dahstini Wash, Tohache Wash, San Juan River and Cowboy Wash.\n\nRivers and streams will continue to rise through the night, and\nare expected to peak Friday afternoon.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMexican Hat, Tselakai Dezza, Bluff, Halchita, Montezuma Creek and\nAneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T09:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.763d446a9fdba9e0de9442d4ef21e6ebf1254b09.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.763d446a9fdba9e0de9442d4ef21e6ebf1254b09.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 12:53PM MDT until October 23 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...South Central Ouray County in southwestern Colorado...\nNorth Central San Juan County in southwestern Colorado...\nEast Central San Miguel County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT Tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1250 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain due to thunderstorms. Flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly in the warned area. Between 1.5 and 2.5 inches\nof rain have fallen over the last 24 hours so any heavy rainfall\non already saturated areas could result in rockslides or\nmudslides in already steep terrain.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nTelluride, Mountain Village, Ouray, Ophir, Camp Bird, Black Bear\nPass and Red Mtn.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Ouray, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.84